        "like": 4
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It seems an application restart is required for the effects to work properly or something. Now I do see a slight improvement in my test scene, but lowering the count further to 2 or 3 cores lowers performance drastically. SMT is disabled in all scenarios. 30% seems very extreme though, and I'm curious if you could show frame time graphs of it.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "5fbb8632b634b41df976891c",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5f2cc9743e5e4b3102c1074e",
        "alias": "Modest Firefly",
        "aliasID": "65c321b0ed6eefce4c45bf28",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny-assets.io/images/92656aa713dfa2908cb8dc64f3c8615a.png",
        "created": "2020-08-07T03:24:36.972Z",
        "name": "~Shizue~",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2020-11-23T09:51:46.233Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [
        "https://canny.io/images/90d818196c56944d47e561d69abb48cb.png"
      ],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "likeCount": 1,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5fb95ff8b1ffed6d116675e0",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 3
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "So I decided to take a look and on a R5 2600 it did have performance benefits, but whether or not that came from limiting the core count or the game running on a single CCX is not for certain.\nThis was also only concluded when the game was running at high FPS. Whether or not this makes a notable difference in normal gameplay at about 90 FPS or in VR is not clear.\nRegardless saw about a 7% uplift in performance and about 10% if core parking was on (increasing clock speeds from 3.7 GHz to 3.9 GHz for the duration of the test), your 30% performance increase claim seems way too high without further evidence to prove it.\nTesting was done in a private instance in void club under as similar conditions as possible.\nAdditionally here's 4 pictures showing the frame time graphs of each test in the picture below.\nhttps://imgur.com/a/UdTCP88",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
