      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": "5fb9c3c2b1ffed6d1167d04e",
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5fb95ff8b1ffed6d116675e0",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5c9ef183b51f4e0393a812e8|full_name}: The 3950X only has 4 core CCXs, there's two 4 core CCXs per 8 core CCD. It's the Ryzen 5000 series that has 8 core CCXs.\nI tried this on my 5950X by limiting VRChat to the first 8C/16T and got a decent performance boost in some situations. It's especially noticeable in medium load situations with high FPS caps like Index at 144Hz. There's still an effect under heavier loads but it seems like it's not quite as noticeable.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
